            <ArticleTitle>Spinal opioids in postoperative pain relief 1: pharmacology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>26-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a two-part unit on using spinal opioids to manage postoperative pain. Part 1 outlines the pharmacology and adverse effects. For details on spinal anatomy and dose levels, plus a table that outlines the differences between spinal anaesthesia and analgesia, and epidural analgesia, see Portfolio Pages at nursingtimes.net.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
